@page "/components/rich-text"
@using Stil.Docs.Examples.RichText

<DocsHeader Title="Rich text" Eyebrow="Writing">
    <Lead>Formatted text for people who do not write Markdown, safe to store and show.</Lead>
</DocsHeader>

<p>
    <code>Stil.RichText</code> is a package of its own, built on AngleSharp and <a href="components/markdown">Stil.Markdown</a>:
    <code>dotnet add package Stil.RichText --prerelease</code> and <code>@@using Stil.RichText</code>. Everything the editor
    sends and the view shows goes through <code>StilRichText.Sanitize</code>, which keeps paragraphs, line breaks, bold,
    italic, underline, strikethrough, headings, lists, links, quotes and code, drops every attribute except a safe link
    address, and removes scripts and embedded content. It writes the HTML anew from the parsed document, so nothing from
    the input is copied through.
</p>

<h2 id="editor">Write and show</h2>
<DocExample Type="typeof(ProductDescription)">
    <p>
        <code>StilRichTextEditor</code> binds like a field and works with EditForm validation; empty text is null. Its
        toolbar has bold, italic, heading, lists, quote, code, link and clear formatting, and Ctrl+B, Ctrl+I and Ctrl+K
        work in the text. Paste from Word, Google Docs or a web page: the structure is kept and the rest is left out.
        <code>Format="StilRichTextFormat.Markdown"</code> stores Markdown instead of HTML. <code>StilRichTextView</code>
        shows saved HTML or Markdown with Stil's typography, also in static SSR. The editor needs an interactive render
        mode.
    </p>
</DocExample>

<h2 id="server">On the server</h2>
<p>
    <code>StilRichText.Sanitize(html)</code> cleans HTML from anywhere, <code>ToMarkdown(html)</code> and
    <code>FromMarkdown(markdown)</code> convert, and <code>HasText(html)</code> tells whether there is any visible text.
</p>

